      "npm_advisory_id": null,
      "overview": "Self-hosted Next.js applications that use the Pages Router with statically generated (SSG) or incrementally regenerated (ISR) pages can have a page's cache entry replaced with content from a different route, causing the affected page to serve wrong content to every visitor until the entry is revalidated. Applications deployed on Vercel are not affected.",
      "reported_by": null,
      "title": "Next.js has cache poisoning of SSG and ISR pages in self-hosted applications",
