      "created": "2026-10-07T20:30:55.000Z",
      "id": 1241496,
      "npm_advisory_id": null,
      "overview": "## Impact\n\nAn attacker-controlled, allow-listed remote URL can lead to server-side request forgery (e.g. to private IPs) during Image Optimization. \n\n## Workaround\n\nAudit allow-listed remote URLs in `images.remotePatterns` (see https://nextjs.org/docs/app/getting-started/images#remote-images) for hosts that may not be trusted with their DNS entries. If no `images.remotePatterns` are configured, your app is not affected.",
      "reported_by": null,
      "title": "Next.js has Server-Side Request Forgery in Image Optimization",
      "metadata": null,
      "cves": [
